{
  "manufacturer": "RenewAire",
  "manufacturer_slug": "renewaire",
  "model": "Premium Commercial Controls (Legacy, v3.xx)",
  "model_slug": "premium-controls-legacy",
  "aliases": [
    "RenewAire Premium Controls legacy",
    "Premium Commercial Controls v3",
    "Carel c.pCO Mini",
    "105999"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy recovery ventilator (ERV) controller (Carel c.pCO, legacy)",
  "applies_to": "Older RenewAire commercial ERVs (HE1.5-8X, LE-Series and RD-Series) with Premium Commercial Controls version 3.xx (Carel c.pCO Mini plus c.pCOe expansion module).",
  "summary": "The legacy Premium Commercial Controls manual covers older RenewAire ERVs on Premium controls v3.xx, a Carel c.pCO Mini with c.pCOe expansion that talks BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP once a BACnet license is installed. Its object map is smaller than the current one (no DOAS reheat, unoccupied or alarm-limit objects). Writes go straight to Present_Value (no priority array).",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Premium controls v3.xx",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Use this list only for older ERVs on Premium controls v3.xx (manual 105999). Current ERV and DOAS controls use manual 147641 (premium-controls), which adds many objects.",
    "Differences from the current map: AI 30/31 are Space_Pressure / Duct_Press, BI 514/521 are named Al_SA_StaticPress / Al_EA_StaticPress, BI 71 is boost status, and BI 560 is the OA filter / BI 561 the RA filter (swapped in the current list). There is no BV 63 unoccupied command.",
    "Retained (EEPROM) points are marked '(retained)' in the descriptions.",
    "The table repeats some alarms under two instances: BI 22/23 and BI 510/511, BI 50 and BI 504.",
    "The file name says 105999_010_D01_JUN25; the back cover prints 105999_010_MAY25."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Premium Commercial Controls Installation, Operation and Maintenance Manual (Legacy)",
    "doc_number": "105999_010_D01_JUN25",
    "revision_date": "2025-06",
    "url": "https://renewaire.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Premium-Controls-User-Man_LEGACY_105999_010_D01_JUN25.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Install the BACnet license, pick BACnet IP or MS/TP as the BMS type and cycle power. Turn on BMS control at the keypad, then start and stop the unit with BV 10. Read BI 21 and MI 7 for status and BI 72 / BI 17 for alarms. Writes land directly on Present_Value with no priority array, and setpoints marked retained should not be written in a loop.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 10",
        "name": "OnOffUnitMng.BmsOnOff",
        "why": "Run/stop command (1 = on)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 55",
        "name": "Occ_HTG_Setp.Val",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, °F (retained)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 56",
        "name": "Occ_CLG_Setp.Val",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, °F (retained)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 80",
        "name": "BMS_SupplyFanCommand",
        "why": "Supply fan speed, 0-100 % (BMS direct mode)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 81",
        "name": "BMS_ExhaustFanCommand",
        "why": "Exhaust fan speed, 0-100 % (BMS direct mode)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 12",
        "name": "AlarmMng.AlrmResByBms",
        "why": "Alarm reset (1 = reset; the unit clears it)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 21",
        "name": "UnitOn",
        "why": "Unit running status (1 = on)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 7",
        "name": "UnitStatus_BN",
        "why": "Operating state, or why the unit is off"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 72",
        "name": "Any_Alarm_Out.Val",
        "why": "Any active alarm"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BMS control of on/off is switched on at the keypad (first BMS screen). Once on, the unit will not start until the BMS writes BV 10 = On, so enable it only when the BMS is ready. The unit also needs the start/stop digital input closed, the keypad set On, the scheduler (if used) in an ON period and no serious alarm; any of these can stop it.",
    "heartbeat": "No BACnet timeout setting is documented. BI 503 Al_BMS_Offline flags that the BMS is offline and clears itself (auto reset); the manual does not say what the unit does then and documents no keep-alive write.",
    "remote_sensors": "AV 53 BMS_CO2_Reading takes a CO2 value from the BMS in place of a wired sensor. AV 54 is named BMS_Space_Press_Reading but the table describes it as a coil leaving-air setpoint for dehumidification, so check it on site. The BMS can also force heat or cool: set BV 60 to Allow, then write BV 61 (0 = heat, 1 = cool).",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet needs a BACnet license file (.ap1, ordered against the controller's Hardware ID), installed from the controller web page Upgrade tab or a USB stick folder named UPGRADE.",
      "BMS settings are in the keypad's General Settings menu after the scheduler. BMS type: None, BACnet MS/TP, BACnet IP, Modbus RTU or Modbus IP; the BACnet choices appear only once the license is installed. Cycle controller power after changing it.",
      "BACnet IP: RJ45 port on the controller. For a static address turn DHCP off, enter IP, mask and gateway, set Update? to Yes and cycle power. Only private address ranges (10.x, 172.x, 192.x) are supported. Device ID is entered digit by digit.",
      "BACnet MS/TP: set Device ID, MAC, baud, Max Master and Max Info Frames. Wire to the 4-pin J3 Disp connector (+, -, GND); it is shared with the remote display, so both can't be used at once, and +Vterm is not used.",
      "The manual gives no default device instance or MAC address."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Points marked retained (EEPROM) survive power loss. Writing them repeatedly raises BI 500/501 (too many writes to retained memory) and can damage the controller. For fan speed loops use AV 80/AV 81 (firmware 03_00_26 and later), with the fan in constant-speed mode and its BMS direct option set to Yes.",
      "Priority_Array is not supported: a BMS write goes straight to Present_Value and a later keypad change overwrites it (last one wins).",
      "Exhaust-fan-only mode: the application notes point to BV 74 (UnitOnOffMng.BMSEFOnly), but the object table has BV 11 OnOffUnitMng.BmsEfOnly for that and BV 74 as the hot-water valve permission. Confirm on the unit.",
      "To drive the hot-water valve from the BMS, set BV 74 to Allow (or Valve Control = BMS at the keypad), then write AV 34 (0-100 % = 0-10 V) and BV 75.",
      "Older firmware wrote through the priority array with a smaller object map; a Pri Array legacy setting keeps that old map, which is not this list.",
      "Which setpoints matter depends on the fan control types (MI 2, MI 3) and the heating and cooling options fitted."
    ]
  },
